<title>SINGAPORE: Superbowl 1996 net profit down 14.14 pct.</title>
<headline>Superbowl 1996 net profit down 14.14 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>(in millions of S$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit				6.00 vs   6.99</p>
<p>    Dividend (pct)			  5.00 vs   5.00</p>
<p>    Group shr (cents)		     3.67 vs   4.28</p>
<p>    Turnover				 41.59 vs  35.43</p>
<p>    Other income incl interest	  0.20 vs   0.37</p>
<p>    Depreciation (expense)		8.14 vs   5.40</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			  9.69 vs  11.39</p>
<p>    Tax					 3.68 vs   4.39</p>
<p>    Dividend pay date:		    July 29, 1997</p>
<p>    Late date books open:		 July 14, 1997</p>
<p>Note - Sports and leisure company Superbowl Holdings Ltd said losses were due mainly to an increase in operating expenses and start-up losses from new businesses.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703305)</p>
</text>
